<title>CANADA: TENNIS-RESULTS MONDAY AT CANADIAN OPEN.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-RESULTS MONDAY AT CANADIAN OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the $2.3 million</p>
<p>Canadian Open men's tennis tournament Monday (prefix number</p>
<p>denotes seeding):</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p>Justin Gimelstob (U.S.) beat 9-Petr Korda (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Sebastien LeBlanc (Canada) beat 10-Tim Henman (Britain) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-3) 4-6 6-3</p>
<p>12-Jonas Bjorkman (Sweden) beat Bobby Kokavec (Canada) 6-3</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>13-Wayne Ferreira (South Africa) beat Daniel Vacek (Czech</p>
<p>Republic) 7-6 (7-5) 6-1</p>
<p>16-Jan Siemerink (Netherlands) beat Leander Paes (India) 6-3</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Tommy Haas (Germany) beat Daniel Nestor (Canada) 5-7 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Chris Woodruff (U.S.) beat Jocelyn Robichaud (Canada) 7-6</p>
<p>(9-7) 6-3</p>
<p>Vince Spadea (U.S.) beat Lionel Roux (France) 3-6 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Jonathan Stark (U.S.) beat Sargis Sargisian (Armenia) 6-7</p>
<p>(3-7) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Marcos Ondruska (South Africa) beat Grant Stafford (South</p>
<p>Africa) 4-6 7-5 6-2</p>
<p>Doug Flach (U.S.) beat Jerome Golmard (France) 7-6 (7-0) 6-4</p>
<p>Neville Godwin (South Africa) beat Byron Black (Zimbabwe) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-2) 4-6 6-4</p>
<p>Scott Draper (Australia) beat Thierry Champion (France) 4-6</p>
<p>6-1 6-2</p>
<p>Geoff Grant (U.S.) beat Eyal Ran (Israel) 7-6 (11-9) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-0)</p>
</text>
